{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview","id":1241136,"title":"Lunars Preview!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-31T20:17:30-07:00","id":1241136,"title":"Lunars Preview!","content":"So, in case you weren't keeping up with the 20 page Lunar Playtest thread (that is upholding the storied tradition of Lunar Threads) a straight up Lunars Preview dropped! (I wasn't, I actually first realized this existed because of a post on FivePoles, but the playtest thread was the only place I saw it mentioned)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lunars-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lunars-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\"> Lunars Preview [Exalted] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lunars-preview-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/lunars-preview-exalted/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It may be due to the fact that I still have the sense of humor of a 12 year old, but how succinct and nonchalant the flavor text for Heart-Drinking Allure is made me giggle.<br /> <br /> The corollary that Memory-Drinking Meditation requires you to keep an intimacy of your targets to maintain their memories is flavorful and fun. Maintaining the memories of all of your victims carries a price on your personality and that is awesome.<br /> <br /> Devil-Pleasing Chiminage is straight up a fun session hook, with weight in the social system, and also made me break out my dictionary.<br /> <br /> I knew that there had been some cards tipped on Steel Paw Style, but I don't know if the fact that it could only be done with certain weapons was known. Regardless I think that's a smart move, although there is another Lunars Thread<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2122</span></span></span> going on right now related to this style of charm that I also stopped following.<br /> <br /> Stalking Nightmare Hunter is bonkers awesome. WOLFMAN FREDDY KRUEGER IS GONNA TAKE YOUR SHAPE. Am I missing something, or is this for permsies too?<br /> <br /> So a nice taste of some of the alternative methods to steal human forms, and some nice displays of Lunar power. I was hoping for a peak at some of the beastman making, territory, or cache charms, but we have to save something for the actual book I guess.<br /> <br /> All in all I would say they felt very Lunar-y, for whatever given value you have for that. I enjoyed them, and found they clearly presented their effects.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T20:47:31-07:00","id":1241148,"title":"","content":"I'm more interested for the sheer amount of conspiratorial fuckery Heart-Drinking Allure allows.<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean, I don't have an alibi, I was <i>right at my post, </i>ask the crew! Everyone saw me!&quot; (<i>Hoo boy, Sweet Thing's gonna be pissed I left the requisition orders to him.</i>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T21:54:30-07:00","id":1241166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview#post1241136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping for a peak at some of the beastman making, territory, or cache charms, but we have to save something for the actual book I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that &quot;MAGPIE'S NEST RESOURCEFULNESS&quot; is one of those Cache Charms, since Cache Charms are Wits-based, the name references a nest, and the effect is that you might always have something useful and relevant tucked away on your person.<br /> <br /> Also, the prerequisite Squirrel's Cunning Technique sounds like the new &quot;I store stuff in Elsewhere&quot; Charm, like a squirrel stuffing a large nut into its cheek.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T23:14:41-07:00","id":1241185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241166#post1241166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure that &quot;MAGPIE'S NEST RESOURCEFULNESS&quot; is one of those Cache Charms, since Cache Charms are Wits-based, the name references a nest, and the effect is that you might always have something useful and relevant tucked away on your person.<br /> <br /> Also, the prerequisite Squirrel's Cunning Technique sounds like the new &quot;I store stuff in Elsewhere&quot; Charm, like a squirrel stuffing a large nut into its cheek.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent point. I'll rephrase that to hoping for some of the more <i>out there </i>cache charms. This is a solid foundation, and cool and helpful power on its own, but I'm really curious to see what the heights of these powers are, especially because it has it's own tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T00:48:14-07:00","id":1241195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview#post1241136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stalking Nightmare Hunter is bonkers awesome. WOLFMAN FREDDY KRUEGER IS GONNA TAKE YOUR SHAPE.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had an image of a Lunar (not Leviathan) who has gotten a bit of a reputation as a wandering deadly sea creature (not necessarily a monster, a large whale would do). One that people don't know is a Lunar, and strictly fear as something known to hunt ships. When the Lunar lets itself be sighted, stalking a ship and making the occasional pass at it, they can smell the fear of the sailors, and knows which ones are feeling it the most.<br /> <br /> Over the next few nights, those sailors will have the worst kinds of dreams; really weird, abstract dreams, rendering their fear of the sea creature in surreal, abstract forms, things that don't correspond to the reality of being hunted at sea at all (everything's all inky and there are rooms with doors that don't go anywhere), or where other anxieties in their life are made analogous to it, and often ending with the person falling through some weird void into the waiting jaws of the beast.<br /> <br /> The Lunar proceeds to use its new library of shapes to wash itself ashore on the various ports that the sailors had been visiting, spreading stories of their ship having been attacked by the beast, and being the only survivor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing something, or is this for permsies too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless there's going to be a blanket rule at the start saying that such powers have a time limit, it would seem to be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T01:10:00-07:00","id":1241198,"title":"","content":"Neat. Although, looking at it, would Stalking Nightmare be compatible with Memory Drinking Meditation? MDM (eh?) calls out the Sacred Hunt specifically, so I wonder how much that is supposed to be mechanically binding, or if it is just fancy wording for taking something's shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T01:50:08-07:00","id":1241204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241198#post1241198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, looking at it again, I'm unsure. Both because it says that the duration of it is &quot;One Dream&quot;, which really feels like a bit of a throwback in terms of designating Charm durations, and in the inference that you would use it repeatedly on the same person.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure there can be the point of repeatedly using it to deny recovering Willpower, but at the moment it still feels a bit ambiguous.<br /> <br /> The duration actually bugs me a bit, because the effects feel to me as though it should just be Instant; I'm pretty sure that there are already Instant Charms whose effects still take a while to unfold, and this thing of &quot;the Charm's Duration is how long it takes to work, and not how long its effect lasts&quot; has been a bad show every time that it turns up, in my opinion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T01:56:59-07:00","id":1241206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241185#post1241185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Excellent point. I'll rephrase that to hoping for some of the more <i>out there </i>cache charms. This is a solid foundation, and cool and helpful power on its own, but I'm really curious to see what the heights of these powers are, especially because it has it's own tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The charms they've previewed are pretty low-level: Essence 1+2, with I think just 1 or 2 Essence 3 charms. I assume that's deliberate.<br /> My guess is this is near the beginning of the Lunar cache tree, and it may well go into things like making your own Elsewhere den higher up the tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T02:02:38-07:00","id":1241208,"title":"","content":"Speaking of essence, I'm curious as to how they're going to handle the issue of no supernals. Starting at essence 1 without supernal your charm choice is pretty limited, even in a bottom heavy charmset. DBs do okay because they start at essence 2, I wonder what Lunars will do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T02:08:24-07:00","id":1241211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241208#post1241208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what Lunars will do.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've said elsewhere, I think that being able to shapeshift will help with that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T02:18:45-07:00","id":1241214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241211#post1241211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I've said elsewhere, I think that being able to shapeshift will help with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they\u2019ll have to go a bit wide like DBs but with more powerful charms and shape shifting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T03:39:09-07:00","id":1241233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241204#post1241204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, looking at it again, I'm unsure. Both because it says that the duration of it is &quot;One Dream&quot;, which really feels like a bit of a throwback in terms of designating Charm durations, and in the inference that you would use it repeatedly on the same person.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure there can be the point of repeatedly using it to deny recovering Willpower, but at the moment it still feels a bit ambiguous.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no ambiguity. The last line is explicit that you <i>can not</i> use it against the same target more than once per story.<br /> <br /> The purpose of the charm is not to harrass someone, it is to attempt to <i>steal their shape</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 08-01-2018, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T03:55:48-07:00","id":1241235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241233#post1241233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no ambiguity. The last line is explicit that you <i>can not</i> use it against the same target more than once per story.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I say ambiguous, I mean that the very idea that you would use it more than once makes whether or not the shape changing is permanent unclear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The purpose of the charm is not to harrass someone, it is to attempt to <i>steal their shape</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so how long do you keep their shape for?<br /> <br /> If you keep the shape forever, <i>why would you use it more than once against the same person!!!</i><br /> <br /> If the Duration actually <i>does</i> mean that you only keep the shape for as long as the person is dreaming, then it sure seems like a very limited Charm.<br /> <br /> And if the Charm grants you a shape permanently, then the Duration should be Instant, because Duration is supposed to be about how long the effect lasts for.<br /> <br /> Like, we <i>have</i> Instant Charms that create simple actions that take a dramatic length of time to unfold, but create effects that are permanent. Why do we have something like this again?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T04:15:43-07:00","id":1241240,"title":"","content":"This question may already have been answered but how many month have passed between the first Dragon-Blooded previews and its Kickstarter ?<br /> <br /> Just to get a vague idea of when we could hope the Lunar's Kickstarter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:02:21-07:00","id":1241250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241235#post1241235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say ambiguous, I mean that the very idea that you would use it more than once makes whether or not the shape changing is permanent unclear.<br /> <br /> Okay, so how long do you keep their shape for?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you steal their shape, it goes into your shape library.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241235#post1241235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you keep the shape forever, <i>why would you use it more than once against the same person!!!</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You cannot use it more than once. You get one dream to <i>attempt</i> to hunt their shape. If it fails, you have to try something else.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241235#post1241235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Duration actually <i>does</i> mean that you only keep the shape for as long as the person is dreaming, then it sure seems like a very limited Charm.<br /> <br /> And if the Charm grants you a shape permanently, then the Duration should be Instant, because Duration is supposed to be about how long the effect lasts for.</div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The duration clearly means you have to commit the 10 motes until the target next sleeps or lose the opportunity to hunt.</span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241235#post1241235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, we <i>have</i> Instant Charms that create simple actions that take a dramatic length of time to unfold, but create effects that are permanent. Why do we have something like this again?</div> </div> </div> </div>More to the point, we have <i>Indefinite</i> duration charms, which last until the exalted disolves the effect or a trigger occurs. This seems to a variation on that, where the trigger is listed in the Duration field.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:27:54-07:00","id":1241252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241250#post1241250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you steal their shape, it goes into your shape library.<br /> [LEFT][COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]You cannot use it more than once. You get one dream to <i>attempt</i> to hunt their shape. If it fails, you have to try something else.<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The duration clearly means you have to commit the 10 motes until the target next sleeps or lose the opportunity to hunt.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>I find these to be reasonable and consistent ideas for how the Charm functions, although I would maintain that if they're the intent, the text itself could do with being more clear on them. My apologies for the overreaction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[LEFT][COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]More to the point, we have <i>Indefinite</i> duration charms, which last until the exalted disolves the effect or a trigger occurs. This seems to a variation on that, where the trigger is listed in the Duration field.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying to read it as the acquisition of the shape not being the effect, but establishing the link that would create the shared dream space being such, at the end of which the Lunar either has acquired a shape or hasn't. If they have, a reference to duration is unnecessary, because by default Lunars retain shapes permanently. Am I reading you correctly?<br /> <br /> I'm suddenly considering that clarification in the text may be unnecessary, if some of these parameters will be already conveyed in the basic shapeshifting and form acquisition rules. That may be something that has come up in discussion of the playtest document, which I am studiously avoiding.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'm satisfied that my query and uncertainty has been resolved, and thank you for responding to me patiently and reasonably.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:38:51-07:00","id":1241254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241240#post1241240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This question may already have been answered but how many month have passed between the first Dragon-Blooded previews and its Kickstarter ?<br /> <br /> Just to get a vague idea of when we could hope the Lunar's Kickstarter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Given the various issues and how the whole book needed to be more or less rewritten, I don't think it'd be a great indicator. Unless you mean the previews for the new (current) material?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:45:47-07:00","id":1241258,"title":"","content":"I don't believe that we got Dragon Blooded previews until after the change in developers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:49:08-07:00","id":1241261,"title":"","content":"That would make the most sense. IIRC Vance and Minton got a redlined first draft handed to them upon being instated as devs, which they then re-redlined for consistency's sake. <br /> <br /> So given that that's roughly where lunars is at the moment, it's probably the best (but by no means great) indication of how long this will take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T05:55:10-07:00","id":1241265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241235#post1241235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you keep the shape forever, why would you use it more than once against the same person!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you would like to use Memory-Drinking Meditation on them again, or a similar Charm. Maybe you dropped the copied Intimacy too soon and there was something more to learn, or you need to learn something about a different person they know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T06:18:36-07:00","id":1241274,"title":"","content":"Or torment them again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T06:52:54-07:00","id":1241284,"title":"","content":"Okay, that line of inquiry has already been resolved, but to reiterate, my question on why the Charm would have a use limit was in response to somebody else asserting that the primary use was in acquiring shapes.<br /> <br /> And I'm reasonably convinced by their point that the main utility of the limit is in not being able to spam attempts if the dream hunt should fail.<br /> <br /> Making the use limit be contingent on other Charms would seem like a really weird design choice, and I find it doubtful that it <i>could</i> be used to drink memories repeatedly, as I'm pretty sure that the only time you get to use that Charm is when a shape is acquired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T06:58:45-07:00","id":1241287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241274#post1241274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or torment them again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, everyone needs a hobby.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T06:59:39-07:00","id":1241289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241284#post1241284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that line of inquiry has already been resolved, but to reiterate, my question on why the Charm would have a use limit was in response to somebody else asserting that the primary use was in acquiring shapes.<br /> <br /> And I'm reasonably convinced by their point that the main utility of the limit is in not being able to spam attempts if the dream hunt should fail.<br /> <br /> Making the use limit be contingent on other Charms would seem like a really weird design choice, and I find it doubtful that it <i>could</i> be used to drink memories repeatedly, as I'm pretty sure that the only time you get to use that Charm is when a shape is acquired.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I saw the Duration and the restriction on repeated use as being tied to the fact that the Charm is not a perfect attempt to achieve a shape, considering it involves a dice roll that can fail, unlike the other Heart-Drinking Allure Charm which has no chance to fail.<br /> <br /> I think the differences between the two shape-stealing Charms lies in the fact that Heart-Drinking Allure requires proximity in the moment of shape stealing, whereas Stalking Nightmare Hunter can occur at a distance, at any point during a week's span of the moment of the target being spooked by your activity, and thus obfuscates the Lunar's involvement making it harder to recognize what a Lunar is doing.<br /> <br /> A use case being here, targeting a noble that usually hides in a fortress, except for some hunting expeditions they do, where you spook the noble but deliberately leave them alive so they can return to their fortress leaving no one the wiser that your real goal is to allow you to take the noble's shape for purposes elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you want your target to be alive still, so they have to deal with the mess arising from what you've done while wearing their shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T07:08:48-07:00","id":1241290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241208#post1241208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of essence, I'm curious as to how they're going to handle the issue of no supernals. Starting at essence 1 without supernal your charm choice is pretty limited, even in a bottom heavy charmset. DBs do okay because they start at essence 2, I wonder what Lunars will do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance did mention on the discord that Lunars have a lot more E 1 charms compared to solars but did not give a exact number.<br /> <br /> Personally I am hoping for a pyramid shape to the charm cascades, since frankly I have never got close to E4 so anything above E3 kind of feels like wasted word space without a supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T07:11:40-07:00","id":1241294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241289#post1241289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I saw the Duration and the restriction on repeated use as being tied to the fact that the Charm is not a perfect attempt to achieve a shape, considering it involves a dice roll that can fail, unlike the other Heart-Drinking Allure Charm which has no chance to fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might depend on what the overall mechanics of the sacred hunt are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the differences between the two shape-stealing Charms lies in the fact that Heart-Drinking Allure requires proximity in the moment of shape stealing, whereas Stalking Nightmare Hunter can occur at a distance, at any point during a week's span of the moment of the target being spooked by your activity, and thus obfuscates the Lunar's involvement making it harder to recognize what a Lunar is doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume that the main differences are that Heart-Drinking Allure only slightly modifies the resolution of a sacred hunt, while Stalking Nightmare Hunter creates one out of whole cloth along different parameters, and the fact that it needs to beat Resolve is because the target needs <i>some</i> potential avenue of escape or resistance, so that it's reasonably balanced against other forms of sacred hunt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T07:28:36-07:00","id":1241301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241294#post1241294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That might depend on what the overall mechanics of the sacred hunt are.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I presume that the main differences are that Heart-Drinking Allure only slightly modifies the resolution of a sacred hunt, while Stalking Nightmare Hunter creates one out of whole cloth along different parameters, and the fact that it needs to beat Resolve is because the target needs <i>some</i> potential avenue of escape or resistance, so that it's reasonably balanced against other forms of sacred hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do see what you mean there. It entirely depends on what the Sacred Hunt mechanic actually is, and that can impact how these Charms fit into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T08:00:06-07:00","id":1241309,"title":"","content":"I like how this preview implies that alternatives ways to gain a shape other than just eating someone will be much easier compared to 2e. Legends of how the anathema can take your shape by bedding you (true), giving you a cursed item (false), etc would fit well for Lunars IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--Lurker Extraordinaire!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/344-darkwolff","name":"DarkWolff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T10:03:09-07:00","id":1241360,"title":"","content":"It would be neat if Lunars could use Sacred Hunts that don\u2019t result in the target\u2019s death to inflict one of the Lunar\u2019s forms upon them in addition to stealing their form.<br /> <br /> Further, this forced transformation becomes harder to break if the Lunar immediately assumes their form. The curse\u2019s greater resilience ends as soon as the Lunar changes again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T10:52:29-07:00","id":1241382,"title":"","content":"No complaints so far about how Lunars are incentivized to commit rape by deception? Frankly, I am surprised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:02:06-07:00","id":1241390,"title":"","content":"Eh, I noticed they've specifically changed the &quot;get forms via sex&quot; to work with a kiss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:21:23-07:00","id":1241398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241382#post1241382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No complaints so far about how Lunars are incentivized to commit rape by deception? Frankly, I am surprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah no, as the charm says \u201cvoluntary act of physical intimacy \u2014 a passionate embrace, a kiss, sex \u2014 instead of killing him.\u201d Key word is Voluntary, and the red rule still applies for PCs. In the case of NPCs I\u2019d also say that this is something that should be discussed between the players and ST before anyone sits down for the first session. So no, they arnt incentivized to commit rape by deception in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Additionally as Wizard noted even a kiss counts, so any decision that a player chooses to do in regards to rape via deception is entirely on the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:54:36-07:00","id":1241421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241398#post1241398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally as Wizard noted even a kiss counts, so any decision that a player chooses to do in regards to rape via deception is entirely on the player.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So is the decision to use Celestial Bliss Trick for rape or Shadow-Immolating Talon for mass torture, yet it did not stop people from complaining about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T13:02:29-07:00","id":1241460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241390#post1241390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I noticed they've specifically changed the &quot;get forms via sex&quot; to work with a kiss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hugs, too. That makes the S-class Lunar hug capability particularly dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:15:12-07:00","id":1241517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241421#post1241421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So is the decision to use Celestial Bliss Trick for rape or Shadow-Immolating Talon for mass torture, yet it did not stop people from complaining about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several key differences between shadow-immolating talon and allure, not the least of which is that SIT does not have a method NOT to deal damage, there are options with allure to not have sex. Secondly, SIT\u2019s mechanics do not have a hard stopper like the red rule in place to protect PCs. Now, for CBT, i think the primary difference is again, CBT only operates through sexual intercourse raises much greater concerns because there is no alternative. This is again, different than allure which operates with any physical intimacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:38:18-07:00","id":1241526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241517#post1241517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are several key differences between shadow-immolating talon and allure, not the least of which is that SIT does not have a method NOT to deal damage, there are options with allure to not have sex. Secondly, SIT\u2019s mechanics do not have a hard stopper like the red rule in place to protect PCs. Now, for CBT, i think the primary difference is again, CBT only operates through sexual intercourse raises much greater concerns because there is no alternative. This is again, different than allure which operates with any physical intimacy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To me, all three seem like a case of &quot;this Charm has a clearly intended use-case but does not prevent you from abusing it in a way that is creepy and wrong, and you even profit by doing so&quot;.<br /> <br /> Granted, Allure grants you the same benefit you would receive by <s>not being</s> being <i>less of </i>a creepy bastard, so it arguably does not reward you for being particularly disgusting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:45:16-07:00","id":1241530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241526#post1241526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To me, all three seem like a case of &amp;quot;this Charm has a clearly intended use-case but does not prevent you from abusing it in a way that is creepy and wrong, and you even profit by doing so&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Granted, Allure grants you the same benefit you would receive by <s>not being</s> being <i>less of </i>a creepy bastard, so it arguably does not reward you for being particularly disgusting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but that arguability is the sticking point. A person has to go out of their way to be a disgusting bastard with allure, where as with SIT and CBT the lack of alternative pathways is a sever limiter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:48:02-07:00","id":1241534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241382#post1241382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No complaints so far about how Lunars are incentivized to commit rape by deception? Frankly, I am surprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. What exactly are we considering rape by deception? I've always considered it to be pretending to be a loved one to have sex with them, without realizing you're a completely different person. Rather than wanting to look more appealing to a stranger you meet at a bar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:52:34-07:00","id":1241536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241534#post1241534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. What exactly are we considering rape by deception? I've always considered it to be pretending to be a loved one to have sex with them, without realizing you're a completely different person. Rather than wanting to look more appealing to a stranger you meet at a bar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Charm text says &quot;<i>a human that has a Major or Defining Tie of love or lust toward her (or her current shape)</i>&quot; - there's nothing stopping you from nomming on a hot soldier boy, taking his shape, going to his home and having sex with his lover (who believes you to be him) to steal their shape as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:55:29-07:00","id":1241539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241536#post1241536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Charm text says &quot;<i>a human that has a Major or Defining Tie of love or lust toward her (or her current shape)</i>&quot; - there's nothing stopping you from nomming on a hot soldier boy, taking his shape, going to his home and having sex with his lover (who believes you to be him) to steal their shape as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. I suppose it really depends on how far the lunar wants to go to succeed at the task at hand. A charm shouldn't dictate morality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T17:01:23-07:00","id":1241567,"title":"","content":"Boy, I sure can see the value to discussion of noting the absence of a thing you don't actually want for the sake of preemptively complaining about it and getting a shot in at people that aren't present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T17:13:26-07:00","id":1241575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241567#post1241567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boy, I sure can see the value to discussion of noting the absence of a thing you don't actually want for the sake of preemptively complaining about it and getting a shot in at people that aren't present.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Clearly, getting a shot in at people who <i>are </i>present is much loftier and does wonders for raising the standards of the discussion :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T17:19:34-07:00","id":1241578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241421#post1241421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is the decision to use Celestial Bliss Trick for rape or Shadow-Immolating Talon for mass torture, yet it did not stop people from complaining about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait... What\u2019s your point exactly? If the \u201csurprise\u201d you expressed in your first post was the pleasant kind then the best way to address that is to... not address or bring it up at all, so that you don\u2019t yourself start the argument that you\u2019re supposedly impressed hasn\u2019t happened yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T17:21:57-07:00","id":1241579,"title":"","content":"I would point out that in your example, Aluminiumtrioxid, you are the one deliberately choosing to go that far.<br /> <br /> You.<br /> <br /> You could take the loverboy's form by whatever means, go home, kiss his lover goodnight, and leave with his form.<br /> <br /> You are the one going &quot;I AM BEING INCENTIVIZED TO RAPE&quot;. You. There is actually no incentive to go any further than that. The form is not better for it, it is not yours longer for it, you do not get experience for it. There is absolutely nothing pushing you to inflict horrific violation upon someone.<br /> <br /> Saying that Heart-Drinking Allure incentivizes rape is like saying that Iron Whirlwind Attack incentivizes murdering orphans. &quot;I can kill a lot more orphans a lot more efficiently by cutting my way through dozens every turn, clearly this is an orphan-murdering charm.&quot; and the rest of us are just going &quot;Why the fuck are you murdering orphans?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-01-2018, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T17:25:36-07:00","id":1241582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241579#post1241579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would point out that in your example, Aluminiumtrioxid, you are the one deliberately choosing to go that far.<br /> <br /> You.<br /> <br /> You could take the loverboy's form by whatever means, go home, kiss his lover goodnight, and leave with his form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're repeating a point I already made though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T17:27:13-07:00","id":1241584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241582#post1241582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're repeating a point I already made though?</div> </div> </div> </div>So IWA should say it only works on people who have intent to cause you physical harm, to prevent it from being an orphan-murdering charm?<br /> <br /> If your intent was 'taking potshots at people not here' and not 'actually professing offense at the charm' maybe you should wait until the people are here rather than try to essentially argue in their stead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T17:46:43-07:00","id":1241593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241584#post1241584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your intent was 'taking potshots at people not here' and not 'actually professing offense at the charm' maybe you should wait until the people are here rather than try to essentially argue in their stead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there's a subtle difference between &quot;arguing for the same people I'd rather take potshots at&quot; and saying that &quot;to me, there seems to be little functional difference between Heart-Drinking Allure and other Charms that are seen as controversial by some people in the community, even though I disagree with the assertion that the existence of said Charms is, in itself, problematic&quot;.<br /> <br /> There seems to be an assumption of bad faith here - that I either expressed surprise because I wanted to start shit with the people who like the preview, or because I wanted to start shit with the people who disliked Celestial Bliss Trick and/or Shadow-Immolating Talon. It's like the idea that I may have expressed surprise <i>because I was</i> <i>legitimately surprised </i>that the same people who complained about those Charms saw no issue with Heart-Drinking Allure (and the reason for that being that this position seemed incongruous to me) isn't up for consideration?<br /> <br /> To be even more specific: I like to think that the devs are listening to feedback. (They probably are!) Heart-Drinking Allure is a very carefully worded effect - it allows you to do things that range from the not at all unsavory (taking the shape of your lover so you can impersonate them when you hear about an impending assassination attempt, hopefully thwarting it) to the not very nice (seducing someone at a social function, taking a kiss and stealing their shape with it, the latter of which they probably did not consent to) to the outright bastardry (taking the shape of someone you know your real target has feelings for with the specific goal of tricking them into some display of physical intimacy, believing you to be the person whose shape you are wearing) and beyond. However, it does not specifically <i>reward you</i> for being more unsavory, unlike, say, Shadow-Immolating Talon, which refunds its cost if you used on someone who could not have provided you with information, effectively rewarding you with information for hurting randos with no additional risk involved. Intuitively, it seems like the two are therefore very different.<br /> <br /> However, I think that this is a difference in <i>degree</i>, and not <i>kind</i>. Assuming you're not roleplaying a monster, you <i>do not</i> buy Celestial Bliss Trick or Shadow-Immolating Talon with the specific purpose of reaping the mechanical benefits for raping and/or torturing others. The Charms provide a benefit for using them in the not-horrible way, and you buy them because you find the not-horrible uses to be appealing. <i>At this point, your calculus of the Charm's utility should probably stop, shouldn't it?</i> If the effect is good and has a niche beyond the horrible things you can also do with them, having the opportunity to do the horrible thing for even greater benefits shouldn't influence your evaluation of the Charm, should it?<br /> <br /> Heart-Drinking Allure has been worded very carefully, but all that careful wording does is make this dynamic explicit: you can use the Charm to do some above-board stuff, or you can use it to do some real fucking disgusting things, but it does not matter which one do you choose, because the benefit you get is the same. But at the same time, the criticism leveled against CBT/SIT is <i>not </i>that these effects are subpar if you're not using them in the most horrible way imaginable - it's that they allow you to benefit from doing the horrible thing in the first place. But this is also true of Heart-Drinking Allure!<br /> <br /> The devs addressed the complaints of some Charms providing benefits for characters who do horrible things by making sure that the new Charm with some serious potential for abuse does not disproportionately reward characters who do the horrible thing. To me, this does not seem like it addresses the real issue of the people who complain about Charms that reward horrible behavior. Yet it seems to have been working!<br /> <br /> This phenomenon is what I was expressing confusion (or rather, surprise) about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 08-01-2018, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T23:30:41-07:00","id":1241703,"title":"","content":"^ Pro tip: open with this next time. Because yes, your first post did in fact give off every impression of trying to start shit with <i>someone</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T12:43:19-07:00","id":1241994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241593#post1241593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heart-Drinking Allure has been worded very carefully, but all that careful wording does is make this dynamic explicit: you can use the Charm to do some above-board stuff, or you can use it to do some real fucking disgusting things, but it does not matter which one do you choose, because the benefit you get is the same. But at the same time, the criticism leveled against CBT/SIT is not that these effects are subpar if you're not using them in the most horrible way imaginable - it's that they allow you to benefit from doing the horrible thing in the first place. But this is also true of Heart-Drinking Allure!</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot follow your logic in this paragraph.<br /> <br /> You might be making reckless use of the word \u201cbut\u201d, without taking more care to establish parallels for your comparisons and contrasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T13:12:49-07:00","id":1242014,"title":"","content":"You know what else lets you benefit from doing bad things?<br /> <br /> Literally every combat charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T13:49:39-07:00","id":1242040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1241994#post1241994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot follow your logic in this paragraph.<br /> <br /> You might be making reckless use of the word \u201cbut\u201d, without taking more care to establish parallels for your comparisons and contrasts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The flippant answer would be &quot;maybe try reading the paragraph directly preceding it&quot;, but I'll bite.<br /> <br /> The criticism leveled against Celestial Bliss Trick and Shadow-Immolating Talon is that they reward you for doing something extra heinous (rape and torture, respectively).<br /> <br /> I believe that the careful wording on Heart-Drinking Allure is, at least in part, a reaction to the backlash against effects such as these: it allows you to benefit from doing the extra heinous thing, but only to the same extent as somebody else who chooses to merely do the highly questionable thing instead would benefit. It does not offer an additional incentive. (Let's put aside the issue that I, personally, do not find the argument that CBT or SIT offer a particularly strong incentive to use them for rape and torture to be terribly compelling either.)<br /> <br /> However, the argument against CBT and SIT did not spring up about the <i>extent</i> of the benefit a character derives from choosing to behave terribly, compared to a character who limited herself to using the controversial Charms in the ways the developer originally intended; it sprang up because the benefit <i>existed in the first place</i>. Therefore, while I see the practical design difference between those Charms and Heart-Drinking Allure, I am not seeing how someone who earnestly holds the position that CBT/SIT are defective from a design standpoint for allowing a character to benefit from doing something terrible could also believe that Heart-Drinking Allure is fine as written without some degree of cognitive dissonance.<br /> <br /> Which leads us back to my original reaction - surprise at the lack of complaints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T14:38:57-07:00","id":1242066,"title":"","content":"Celestial Bliss Trick doesn\u2019t reward rape. It rewards bringing someone to orgasm, which you can do with the subject\u2019s enthusiastic consent. Your framing is erroneous from the beginning.<br /> <br /> Shadow Immolating Talon can be used in battle against a superior opponent who is curb-stomping you. It rewards you for landing a blow on someone. Again, you are guilty of misleading framing.<br /> <br /> Heart-Drinking Allure doesn\u2019t reward forceful rape not because of any moral concerns, but because such an action is an insufficient challenge. Notice how the Strength Charm for stealing shapes and the Charisma Charm for binding oaths both require the hunter to be clever enough to trick the target into giving consent, and then strong enough to beat them at the contest, clever enough to trap them in an impossible oath, and seductive enough to receive a willing kiss. <br /> <br /> The Charm is horribly open to abusive through acts of rape-by-deception, and actually encourages Lunars to commit such actions.<br /> <br /> There is no moral superiority here, nor do I feel that CBT or SIT were poorly designed or worded in such a way to make them seem worse than they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T15:28:30-07:00","id":1242089,"title":"","content":"Moving on to actual concerns instead of... whatever <i>this</i> is: Anyone else think Magpie\u2019s Nest Resourcefulness could do with its own Orichalcum Rule disclaimer (e.g.- \u201cThe ST may veto anything that there\u2019s no plausible way the Lunar could have gotten her hands on\u201d) like some other charms have? So no one gets any ideas about pulling a silver talent out of their sleeves every scene or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T15:35:24-07:00","id":1242092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1242066#post1242066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial Bliss Trick doesn\u2019t reward rape. It rewards bringing someone to orgasm, which you can do with the subject\u2019s enthusiastic consent. Your framing is erroneous from the beginning.<br /> <br /> Shadow Immolating Talon can be used in battle against a superior opponent who is curb-stomping you. It rewards you for landing a blow on someone. Again, you are guilty of misleading framing.<br /> <br /> Heart-Drinking Allure doesn\u2019t reward forceful rape not because of any moral concerns, but because such an action is an insufficient challenge. Notice how the Strength Charm for stealing shapes and the Charisma Charm for binding oaths both require the hunter to be clever enough to trick the target into giving consent, and then strong enough to beat them at the contest, clever enough to trap them in an impossible oath, and seductive enough to receive a willing kiss.<br /> <br /> The Charm is horribly open to abusive through acts of rape-by-deception, and actually encourages Lunars to commit such actions.<br /> <br /> There is no moral superiority here, nor do I feel that CBT or SIT were poorly designed or worded in such a way to make them seem worse than they are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Literally nothing of what you said addresses anything I said in any way though?<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, let's break it down paragraph by paragraph:<br /> <br /> - You make an argument that my framing of CBT and SIT is &quot;misleading&quot;. Me saying that these Charms <i>have been criticized</i> on the basis that they reward rape/torture could only be misleading if the criticism I was referring to somehow didn't happen. I only repeated that I personally did not agree with this criticism <b>three times</b> over the course of the last few posts I made. I literally have no idea how I could possibly make my stance on this any clearer.<br /> <br /> - You argue that Heart-Drinking Allure doesn't reward forceful rape, attacking a point I <i>did not make</i>. (Alternative, more charitable interpretation: this paragraph is actually part of the same thought as the next one, and you're just explaining that morality has no impact on how Lunar Charms work. Which, while compellingly argued, has nothing to do with anything I said.)<br /> <br /> - You then go on to point out that the Charm is open to abuse through acts of rape by deception, framing this as a counterpoint, <i>as if I wasn't saying the exact same thing twice already</i>. Then you make the questionable assertion that it &quot;encourages Lunars to commit such actions&quot;, the counterargument to which has actually been touched on a page ago. You do not address this counterargument directly, nor do you bring up any compelling evidence that might do so indirectly.<br /> <br /> - Then you conclude that there is no moral superiority here (compared to CBT and SIT, I assume). A point I find arguable, but since I assume it rests on the assertion addressed above, I have no way to meaningfully address your argument for it, because you haven't made one. Then you add that you do not feel CBT or SIT were poorly designed or worded, which, while technically orthogonal to the original observation I made (&quot;while it seems like great care has been taken to word Heart-Drinking Allure in a way that averts the kind of criticism that befell CBT and SIT, I do not think the actual problem people had with those Charms was addressed, which makes me surprised that complaints of similar nature have not yet emerged&quot;), actually seems to <i>expand </i>the scope of what I was referring to, by providing an example of someone who found CBT/SIT unobjectionable while thinking that Heart-Drinking Allure is open to abusive acts and encourages Lunars to commit them.<br /> <br /> <br /> All in all, reading your post is a very strange experience, because while it is framed like you're in opposition of the things I say, it seems like half the time you don't actually engage with any of it, and the other half you seem to be sorta-kinda agreeing with them in a roundabout way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 08-02-2018, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T15:40:07-07:00","id":1242097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1242089#post1242089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving on to actual concerns instead of... whatever <i>this</i> is: Anyone else think Magpie\u2019s Nest Resourcefulness could do with its own Orichalcum Rule disclaimer (e.g.- \u201cThe ST may veto anything that there\u2019s no plausible way the Lunar could have gotten her hands on\u201d) like some other charms have? So no one gets any ideas about pulling a silver talent out of their sleeves every scene or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to check the page again, so could somebody remind me what the use limit of the Charm is?<br /> <br /> I don't think that it's wholly unreasonable, but I think that application needs to have very exacting standards, since I think that half the fun is being able to pull out whatever one wants or is useful.<br /> <br /> Although... I think it could be as simple as money just being a bit too mundane for the Charm. I mean, it's not unreasonable to assume that somebody would be carrying money on their person in any case, it's not really worth spending motes on. I think that this is better suited to things that are more novel or circumstantial.<br /> <br /> \u2026 Wait, a talent? I think that's too large a quantity for the Charm to apply to it. That's about 26 kilos of silver, I don't think that can be hidden so readily. That's not pulling it out of your sleeves so much as holding your sleeve open and a cascade pours out for several seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T15:40:15-07:00","id":1242098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1242089#post1242089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving on to actual concerns instead of... whatever <i>this</i> is: Anyone else think Magpie\u2019s Nest Resourcefulness could do with its own Orichalcum Rule disclaimer (e.g.- \u201cThe ST may veto anything that there\u2019s no plausible way the Lunar could have gotten her hands on\u201d) like some other charms have? So no one gets any ideas about pulling a silver talent out of their sleeves every scene or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having stolen some money prior with a Larceny roll seems like an intended use-case, though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T16:31:37-07:00","id":1242124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1242089#post1242089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving on to actual concerns instead of... whatever <i>this</i> is: Anyone else think Magpie\u2019s Nest Resourcefulness could do with its own Orichalcum Rule disclaimer (e.g.- \u201cThe ST may veto anything that there\u2019s no plausible way the Lunar could have gotten her hands on\u201d) like some other charms have? So no one gets any ideas about pulling a silver talent out of their sleeves every scene or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It has the note 'mundane' so, a talent of <i>metal </i> would be much, but like a bank note? Sounds fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T17:28:06-07:00","id":1242145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1241136-lunars-preview?p=1242124#post1242124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has the note 'mundane' so, a talent of <i>metal </i> would be much, but like a bank note? Sounds fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but a regular counterfeiter can do that, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","dat